Cadillac is a popular luxury car brand with a reputation for quality and performance. However, even the best cars can have issues, and Cadillac vehicles are not immune to defects. It’s just the nature of mass-produced products.

That’s why the Cadillac lemon law exists - to protect consumers from being stuck with a faulty vehicle. These laws provide remedies for those who have purchased or leased a defective Cadillac car (under warranty) that can’t be fixed after being subjected to multiple repair attempts.

In order for your defective Cadillac car to qualify as a lemon in California, it must:

- Be covered under the manufacturer or dealer warranty when the defect or nonconformity was first reported; and

- Have one or more defects/nonconformities that substantially impair the vehicle’s use, value, or safety; and

- Have been subjected to a reasonable number of repair attempts by a manufacturer-certified facility to fix the defect or nonconformity; or

- Have been out of service for repairs on one or more defects/nonconformities for at least 30 days; and

- The defect or nonconformity must not have been caused by driver abuse or neglect.

If your vehicle qualifies as a lemon, you may be entitled to compensation in the form of a [Cadillac buyback](/blog/lemon-law-buybacks-what-to-expect) (refund) or replacement vehicle.

In this post, we will go over the ten most common issues that could rule your vehicle eligible for Cadillac lemon law. Let’s dive right in.

## 1. Transmission Failures

One of the most common issues found in defective Cadillac cars is transmission problems. Common transmission issues include difficulty shifting gears, jerking motions when accelerating, and slipping.

If you experience any of these symptoms with your Cadillac vehicle, it’s important to have it inspected by a manufacturer-certified mechanic as soon as possible. They will be able to determine if the problem is related to the transmission or something else.

If the problem persists and you have gone through multiple attempts to fix it, your vehicle may qualify for a Cadillac buyback or replacement.

## 2. Suspension Issues

Suspension problems can be common in Cadillac vehicles. In fact, over [380,000 defective Cadillac cars](https://www.consumerreports.org/car-recalls-defects/general-motors-recalls-suvs-for-rear-suspension-problem-a8620817999/) were recalled in 2021 due to suspension issues. The most common symptoms of a suspension problem include rattling, clunking, and an overall lack of stability while driving.

If your Cadillac exhibits any of these symptoms, get it inspected as soon as possible. Not only are suspension issues a nuisance, but they can also become extremely dangerous if left unchecked.

## 3. Electrical Problems

Cadillacs are known for their impressive array of modern technology, including advanced infotainment systems and driver-assist features. But unfortunately, these cutting-edge systems can be susceptible to electrical issues that cause a variety of problems.

Common symptoms include intermittent power loss, faulty navigation, and unresponsive touchscreens. If your Cadillac exhibits these symptoms - and is covered under warranty - you should take it to a certified mechanic as soon as possible.

Again, if the issue(s) can’t be resolved after multiple repair attempts, you may have grounds for a Cadillac lemon law claim.

## 4. Airbag Failure

An airbag failure is one of the most dangerous problems a car can experience. If your Cadillac’s airbags don’t deploy correctly in an accident, they may not be able to provide the protection that you need in an accident. This can lead to serious injury or death.

You may receive a recall notice from the manufacturer if there is a recurring issue with your model’s airbag system. Unfortunately, most drivers do not realize their airbag is malfunctioning until after a collision. Do some research on your Cadillac model for any patterns in airbag issues - and get in touch with a certified repair facility to investigate.

If there are problems that can’t be fixed and the airbag defect falls under Cadillac lemon law guidelines, you may be eligible for compensation. Contact a California lemon law attorney to see if you qualify.

## 5. Paint Issues

If your Cadillac is fading, cracking, or peeling, it could be due to a defective paint job. If you’re experiencing any of these issues job, you should have it inspected by a certified technician to determine the root of the problem.

This problem needs to be addressed quickly, as the paint can cause costly damage if left unchecked. California’s lemon law does not typically cover paint issues, but you may be eligible for relief through the manufacturer’s warranty.

## 6. Engine Misfiring

Engine misfiring is a common problem that can cause various issues, such as faulty spark plugs or bad fuel injectors. This can lead to noticeable decreases in performance, as well as increased emissions and fuel consumption.

If your Cadillac is experiencing engine misfiring, take it to a certified mechanic as soon as possible for warranty repairs. Be sure to get all [repair attempts in writing](/blog/california-lemon-law-claim-documents) and keep them in case you need to file a California lemon law case later on.

## 7. Brake Issues

If your brakes are not working properly, it can be dangerous - and potentially deadly. It is important to have them serviced and checked regularly to ensure they are in good working condition. If you experience any issues, such as grinding noises or difficulty stopping, take your car to a certified mechanic right away.

If this problem is not a result of driver abuse or neglect - and it falls under [California lemon law guidelines](https://www.consumer-action.org/downloads/english/CA_lemon_law_2015_EN.pdf) - you may be eligible for a Cadillac buyback. Contact a California lemon law attorney for more information.

## 8. Air Conditioning Issues

If your Cadillac’s air conditioning system is not working properly, it can be a major inconvenience, especially during the summer months. Common causes of air conditioning problems include leaks in the system or low freon levels.

Since this issue interferes with the “use” of your vehicle, it may qualify as a substantial defect under Cadillac lemon law. A [California lemon law lawyer](/) will help determine your legal rights and point you in the right direction.

## 9. Water Leaks

Water leaks can be caused by a number of issues, including faulty door seals or sunroofs that aren’t properly sealed. If you’re experiencing water leaks in your Cadillac, you should have it inspected by a certified technician to determine the cause.

These types of issues can typically be fixed by replacing or re-sealing faulty parts. Don’t wait too long to have it fixed, as water leaks can cause costly damage if left unchecked.

## 10. Window Issues

Power window issues can be caused by faulty motors, switches, or wiring. If your Cadillac’s power windows aren’t working properly, you should have them inspected by a certified technician to determine the cause.

This issue interferes with the functionality and value of your vehicle, so it’s important to have it fixed as soon as possible. If the problem can’t be fixed and you’re covered under warranty, you may be eligible for a buyback or replacement vehicle under Cadillac lemon law.

